     If you are using MUC Light, make sure this option is set to the MUC Light domain
 
+#### `modules.mod_mam.muc.delete_messages_of_removed_users`
+* **Syntax:** boolean
+* **Default:** `false`
+* **Example:** `modules.mod_mam.muc.delete_messages_of_removed_users = true`
+
+When enabled, removing a user account (or purging an anonymous user) also deletes the messages that the user sent to MUC rooms from the room archives.
+By default these messages stay in the room archives after the account is removed.
+Only the `rdbms` backend supports this option.
+
 #### Example
 
 The example below presents how to override common option for `muc` module specifically.
